+# Corpus fetching
+
+The corpus fetch had to respect a per-domain limit of **12 visits in a
+60-second window**. After breaching that limit, the domain entered a
+**900-second (15-minute) cooldown**.
+
+Files were fetched through these hosts:
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com`
+- `cdn.jsdelivr.net`, using paths of the form
+  `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/owner/repo@branch/path`
+- `cdn.statically.io`
+
+`cdn.statically.io` was used as a mirror, but requests to it were slow and
+sometimes timed out. The corpus manifest independently identifies
+`raw.githubusercontent.com` as the raw-file source; the rate-limit values and
+mirror usage above are the values recorded during the actual fetch run.
